{
  "_about": "v79.8 (Block B): the norms that confer an action. A claim candidate («Fondare la domanda sull'art. X», a riconvenzionale) is built only on an article one of these rules admits: an institution module's «actions» (the institution the first read names, or the case's words: «patterns») or a remedies.json matter's «actions». A module's articles come first, in its order (the specific norm before the general one: 2053 before 2051); «general» (1218, 1453, 2043) are subordinate -- offered with a module only when the module yields nothing proven. «limiting» are never a claim (they measure or condition a claim, they confer none). Edit here; lawyer_method.claim_admission reads it. v79.8.5: modules marked «draft» are Code's proposal, for the lawyer's review (famiglia, consumo, lavoro beyond the licenziamento, successioni, condominio). v79.9 (Block B): a module may carry «stages» (the stage its articles differ by, read from the case's certain facts -- «patterns» -- or the events the terms read -- «events»: consegna, fine lavori, scoperta vizio, denuncia/reclamo; the first stage that matches puts its «actions» first), «conditional» actions (offered only when a certain fact matches their patterns: 1439 on a false description), «non_actions» (code articles that are no claim norm for the client: 2118, 2119 for a dismissed worker), «laws» (the special laws that govern it, checked against the graph's primary documents: data/corpus_expected.json holds the same list, with how each is matched), «requires» («professional_counterparty»: the consumer module only with a business as a certain fact) and «name». v79.10 (A4): a module may carry «weak_patterns» and «weak_min» (default 2): with them, the module is active on one of its «patterns» (the strong ones) or on «weak_min» different weak patterns -- «il Comune» alone never activates the amministrativo module (a 2051 custodia case naming the Comune as custodian); a module without «weak_patterns» activates as before, on any pattern. The amministrativo module (draft): L. 241/1990, c.p.a., TU edilizia d.P.R. 380/2001; its «laws» hold L. 241/1990 and the d.P.R. 380/2001 only -- the c.p.a. is a code, always admitted by the family gate (src/rag/family_gate.py). v79.10 (A4, review): «autotutela» is strong only in its administrative form (annullamento / revoca in autotutela, autotutela amministrativa, the Comune's or the administration's in the same sentence) -- never the civil self-help (1460, the tenant's, autotutela contrattuale / possessoria); the weak act needs the ente: a provvedimento the Comune / PA adopts in the same sentence (no judge word in it, never disciplinare) or «del Comune» / comunale / dirigenziale, a diniego of a permesso / autorizzazione / licenza / concessione / istanza / accesso, an ordinanza sindacale, a delibera comunale; «nel Comune di X» (an address) and «(PA)» (a province) are no ente. v79.10 (A4, archive names): the licenziamento module's «laws» hold the Fornero reform L. 92/2012 (in the archive: «Riforma del Lavoro Fornero 2026») beside L. 604/1966, L. 300/1970, d.lgs. 23/2015 and d.lgs. 81/2015 (not in the archive: the missing-laws line names them). A special law's action («7 l. 241/1990») matches the label the pipeline builds for that article of its archive document («7 Legge sul Procedimento Amministrativo 2026»): the action's law is resolved through data/corpus_expected.json «archive_names» (lawyer_method.same_article). v79.12.1: a module switches on only from the first read's institution (its name and rubricated name, never its claim sentence), a module article named in the request (lawyer_method.named_module_articles: never a «general» one) or the user's words -- the institution first, then the user's words, then a named article (review: an incidental article never replaces the module the case's words name), the first that finds one; «context_patterns» are the words a damage or a claim also uses (the hospital, the surgeon, the pronto soccorso after a slap; the heirs' «a titolo ereditario», «coeredi … parte civile», «per successione», «erede legittima» in a homicide; a fall «dalla sedia» after a slap; a «passaggio pedonale»): they count from the first read's institution only, never from the user's words alone -- the module's strong «patterns» name it (testamento, quota di legittima, the coeredi's divisione, a vase fallen from a balcony, a slip on a pothole, the diritto di passaggio, a surgeon's or an operation's harm, an infezione nosocomiale, a claim against the clinic or the ASL); «legittima» is never the legittima difesa and «successione» never the «iure successionis» of a damage claim. Each active module records the signal that switched it on (lawyer_method.active_modules: «signal», «signal_words»).",
